{
 "name": "mountain_giant",
 "_about": "Gallery creature: a menacing mountain giant, 4 m. Heavy hunched biped; the huge fists are the signature.",
 "_notes": [
  "Seventh pass: a STYLISED GAME giant \u2014 a big characterful head on massive shoulders, forearms heavier than the upper arms, a gut, short thick legs with a bent knee, and fists with daylight between the fingers.",
  "The fists are chains, not a 'hand' part: palm (LHand) + four folded fingers (LF1-LF4, knuckle joint b, proximal c runs back, middle d runs up, tip e tucks in) + a thumb. Back of the hand faces forward, knuckles down. Finger radius 0.105 on 0.27 m centres: the engine's digit-fuse warning is silent (it was 83% before).",
  "Fists, fingers and thumb are shade 'hard': the L1 seam blend radius on a 4 m body is ~20 cm, wider than a finger, and it averaged the knuckle row away and painted the knees ochre where the fists hang beside them.",
  "function names RArm/RHand/RF1-4/RThumb explicitly: effector_leads does not count a mirrored chain's twin as the effector (see example/gallery/README.md).",
  "Elbow and knee dips are profile rows AT the joint (\"LElbow\", \"LKnee\"): the engine resolves the t, so the narrowing lands on the joint and not on a guess."
 ],
